      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1880s, freedmen in the Hudson area of Meridian established one of the first commercial shrimping operations in McIntosh County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://vanishinggeorgia.com/category/meridian-ga/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A Union Brothers & Sisters mission was founded in Meridian in 1887, reflecting early African‑American community organization.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://vanishinggeorgia.com/category/meridian-ga/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The current Hudson Home Society building, built around 1900 to replace a fire‑lost original, once served as a schoolhouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://vanishinggeorgia.com/category/meridian-ga/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Meridian’s vernacular hip‑roof cottages are among the last surviving examples of a style once common in African‑American coastal Georgia communities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
